\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 1. Transference of consciousness to new bodies in the sentient plane. }
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 2. The psychology of transference. Once transferred to new sentient counter bodies. There own bodies are preserved in a state of hidden stasis. Undetectable in a space that foregoes and is hidden from the protectant. If the protectant do or were to discover them. Their minds would still have been captured and stored. And thus they would live on. }
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 It could be revealed to them at a later stage that the whole time they were on Oasis, this was done so in a sleeping sentient host which their minds were uploaded to. The Beverley itself would no longer exist. And it would be presented to them that they had been recovered in an unconscious state by a standing by sentient carrier ship.}
\par\plain \f1\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 Slip space and theoretical jump space technology makes no sense. Bending space and time seem like radical ideas in the sense where physical properties are ignored. The distance between space and the physical arrangement of particles and motion all cannot be ignored however the transferrrence of data in rapid long range forms is possible. Transferring data over long distances in packets through beacons is possible and thereby transferrence would be possible to achieve this. This in a sense seems more theoretically feasible. }
